<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bani Utbah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Utub</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bani Utbah were a confederation of Arab clans from central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> that migrated to the Gulf coast in the late 17th and early 18th centuries. Under the protection of the Banu Khalid they settled at Kuwait, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-sabah">Al Sabah</a> became rulers, and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zubarah">Zubarah</a> in Qatar, from where the Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> in 1783. They lived by pearling, shipbuilding and trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bani-utbah.jpg" alt="Bani Utbah" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SPQR10 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pre_Islamic_Arabian_Tribes_(Harold_Dixon).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
